--- selected exact pin ---
## Decision

**Adopt `committed` (crate-ci) at the exact pin `1.1.11` — no range; a later release is accepted only through the upgrade gate stated below — as the Conventional-Commits linter that runs at `commit-msg` time and again in CI**, configured by a repository-root `committed.toml` (plus `committed.bot.toml`, used by CI for bot pull requests). The `commit-message-convention` it enforces is an explicit eleven-member type enum (`build, chore, ci, docs, feat, fix, perf, refactor, revert, style, test`), a 50-column cap on the whole header line (`type(scope): description`, the same span commitlint's `header-max-length` counts; executed as case 21), and a 72-column cap on every body and footer line under soft-line measurement (the exact value is in `## Parameters`). commitlint through a provisioned Node/Bun runtime — both source repos' tool, the Codex report's pick, and the pick of two of the three Doxa provider reports (OpenAI, Perplexity) — is the architectural runner-up and is not adopted. `cargo-commitlint` 2.1.0 — the Gemini provider report's pick and the OpenAI report's runner-up, a native binary with three independent length knobs — was installed and executed against the same fixture (`## Empirical check`); it rejects the bare-URL and trailer lines the contract must accept (comparison cases 05, 07), tests upstream on Linux only, has 3 stars and one human contributor, and ships an installed-hook template that exits 0 when its binary is missing, so it is recorded as a runner-up with conditions, not adopted. `conventional_commits_linter` 0.17.1 — which revision 5 excluded on its licence alone and which re-entered the field unevaluated when the owner struck that gate — was installed at the pin and executed against the same fixture here: it caps the header only, has no body-line and no footer-line rule of any kind, exposes a two-valued type preset rather than a declarable vocabulary, declares no `rust-version`, and ships neither a macOS binary nor a macOS CI job, so it is excluded on capability and on gates 2 and 4, on the executed evidence in `## Empirical check`.

Ledger rows this settles (all `docs/port/COMMONALITY.md:153-161`):

| Row | Settled value |
|---|---|
| F149 commit-msg linter tool | `committed`, exact pin `1.1.11` in every place that names a version (install recipe, `--version` assertion, action SHA); a later release passes the recorded upgrade gate first |
| F150 hook invocation mechanism | `committed --fixup --wip --commit-file {1}` from the hook manager's `commit-msg` stage (`{1}` is the message-file path; R37 wires the stage) |
